From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] the NTSC rate from the exact master clock, not a rounded one

60.0988118623484 is 21477272 / 357366: the master clock rounded down
from 945/44 MHz, six times the NTSC subcarrier, and 0.034 ppm low. The
panel mode this core selects is cut to twice the exact rate, so against
the rounded one it drifts a frame every 63 hours instead of every 824.
The NES shares the SNES's master clock and its 357366 clocks a frame,
so the SNES core gets the same correction.

--- a/Core/NES/NesConsole.cpp
+++ b/Core/NES/NesConsole.cpp
@@ -360,7 +360,9 @@ double NesConsole::GetFps()
 {
 	UpdateRegion();
 	if(_region == ConsoleRegion::Ntsc) {
-		return 60.0988118623484;
+		//945/44 MHz, six times the colour subcarrier, over 357366 master
+		//clocks a frame; 60.0988118623484 was 21477272 Hz, 0.034 ppm low
+		return 945000000.0 / 44.0 / 357366.0;
 	} else {
 		return 50.0069789081886;
 	}
